==Acquisition==
*This mod can be acquired by attaining the rank of '''Maxim''' under {{Faction|Arbiters of Hexis}}, or the rank of '''Partner''' under {{Faction|The Perrin Sequence}}, and spending {{sc|25,000}} to purchase.

==Notes==
*Tap cast grants {{D|Cold}} damage. Hold cast grants {{D|Heat}} damage.
**Both fields can exist simultaneously, granting each elemental buff separately.
**If a player obtains both elemental buffs, they combine into a {{D|Blast}} buff, equaling the sum of {{D|Cold}} and {{D|Heat}} damage.
**Bonus damage does <u>not</u> combine with modded elements, and is ''additive'' with elemental mods.
**Does <u>not</u> affect exalted weapons or warframe abilities.
*Duration is refreshed and paused indefinitely while standing in the Thermal Sunder field.
**{{D|Cold}} and {{D|Heat}} fields refresh the duration of the corresponding buffs, the {{D|Blast}} damage buff duration is paused in any of the fields.
*Sunder areas gain an inward pulsing visual effect to indicate Thermal Transfer is equipped. 
*The caster and allies see the Thermal Transfer {{D|Cold}}, {{D|Heat}}, or {{D|Blast}} bonus as separate buff icons with a value of the elemental damage added and the remaining duration in seconds.
*Elemental Damage bonus scales with {{Stat|Ability Strength}}.
*Buff duration scales with {{Stat|Ability Duration}}
*For status damage purposes {{D|Heat}} bonus is additive with other {{D|Heat}} damage bonuses, while {{D|Blast}} does not contribute towards status damage.

